[
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Some important design lessons from the Therac-25 account include recognizing that timing errors can be hard to reproduce and may underlie serious failures, and that many computer-related accidents arise from requirements faults rather than coding faults.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "They point out that most computer-related accidents result from requirements faults, not from coding faults, and they list several basic software engineering principles that were violated by the Therac-25:",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "The underlying cause of the problems was a timing error that was difficult to reproduce.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Design practices should emphasize early and ongoing documentation, integrated software quality assurance, and the use of standards established at the outset to evaluate intermediate products.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Documentation should be done as development progresses, not afterward.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Software quality assurance practices should be an integral part of the development process. These practices should include standards that are set early and used to evaluate intermediate products.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "The case also highlights the value of redundant safety measures, as reflected in the AECL recommendation to add hardware interlocks to back up software control of energy selection and electron-beam scanning.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "The AECL final report recommended 10 changes to the Therac-25 hardware, including interlocks to back up software control of energy selection and electron-beam scanning.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    }
]

